  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Paula Pacheco",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Kevin Sousa",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T13:19:21-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Kevin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T13:19:24-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi Kevin, it's Paula Pacheco. Sorry, bear with me one sec, I'm on a step stool changing a lightbulb. Okay, I'm good."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T13:19:32-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No worries, don't fall on my account. What can I help you with?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T13:19:37-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So basically, someone in my neighborhood keeps leaving trash bags at the corner. Like four or five black bags, not at anybody's house, just piled by the stop sign. It's been there since the weekend."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T13:19:49-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, trash bags at the corner, since the weekend. Got it. Do you know which corner?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T13:19:55-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, it's Marlborough and Thames, by the stop sign. I'm pretty sure it's a neighbor because I've seen the same bags go out before. I can't prove it though."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T13:20:05-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. I'll put in a request to have it looked at and picked up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T13:20:10-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Great. Is there a fee for that? Like, do I get charged for reporting it or anything?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T13:20:16-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, nothing for you to pay for reporting it. Any cost question would be about whoever dumped it, and that's up to the city once it's reviewed."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T13:20:25-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, perfect. That's all I needed. Thanks, Kevin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T13:20:28-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thanks, Paula. Have a good one."
    }
  ],
